{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ClientAuthMethod"]]},"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ClientAuthMethod\/none"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"sections":[],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/clientauthmethod\/none"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"none"}],"externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK16ClientAuthMethodO4noneyA2CmF","title":"ClientAuthMethod.none","symbolKind":"case","modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}],"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Case"},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"none"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"}],"references":{"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK":{"role":"collection","type":"topic","title":"AxiamSDK","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The official Swift SDK for AXIAM (Access eXtended Identity and Authorization Management)."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/ClientAuthMethod/none":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"none","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/clientauthmethod\/none","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[],"title":"ClientAuthMethod.none","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ClientAuthMethod\/none"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/ClientAuthMethod":{"fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ClientAuthMethod","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"How a client proves its identity at the token endpoint (RFC 8705 §2, OIDC Core §9 naming)."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Only the methods AXIAM actually implements are representable. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"None"},{"type":"text","text":" — the public-client"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value — was deliberately absent until T21.2: adding it before the rest of the server"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"understood one would have let an operator register a client whose authentication is silently"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"skipped. The server understands one now ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"token.rs"},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"authenticate_client_credential"},{"type":"text","text":" has"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an arm that accepts "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"no"}]},{"type":"text","text":" credential and refuses a presented one, the authorization endpoint"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"derives its PKCE requirement from this enum, and the admin API refuses the method alongside"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"any grant or binding that contradicts it), so the variant exists — and only that arm may"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ever treat a missing credential as success."}],"title":"ClientAuthMethod","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ClientAuthMethod","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ClientAuthMethod","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/clientauthmethod"}}}